        "original_id": "7ae90f31-3624-5c26-9bd1-bce531cda747",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: HeroClix, Attacktix, Shadowrun, Marvel Legends Showdown, XEVOZ\n- Systems: Clix system\n- Companies: Capcom, WizKids, Toy Biz, Hasbro\n- Franchises: Street Fighter, Gears of War, Halo, Marvel, DC Comics\n- Topics: collectible miniatures games, collectible action figure games\n\nFacts:\n- HeroClix is a collectible miniatures game that uses the Clix system and centers on superhero comic book worlds, especially Marvel and DC Comics.\n- HeroClix lets players build teams of heroes, villains, and characters from franchises such as Street Fighter, Gears of War, and Halo for turn-based battles on grid maps based on storyline locations.\n- Street Fighter is a fighting video game franchise developed and published by Capcom.\n- Attacktix has been compared to HeroClix.\n- Subsequent collectible action figure games included WizKids' Shadowrun, Toy Biz's Marvel Legends Showdown, and Hasbro's XEVOZ and Attacktix.",
